 ],
 "hooks": [
  "Square plane windows once *killed people.*",
  "Your plane window is round for a *deadly* reason.",
  "One shape *broke* the first jet airliner."
 ],
 "caption": "The first jet airliner had square-cornered windows. In 1954 two of them broke apart in the air. Every plane window since has been rounded.",
 "hashtags": [
  "aviation",
  "engineering",
  "didyouknow",
  "planes",
  "history"
 ],
 "sources": [
  {
   "claim": "The de Havilland Comet flew its first passenger service on May 2, 1952, with square cabin windows. BOAC Flight 781 (January 10, 1954) and South African Airways Flight 201 (April 8, 1954) broke up in flight. Investigators blamed metal fatigue from repeated pressurising, with cracks starting at the square corners of cutouts",
   "source": "Jason Lefkowitz, Why airplane windows have round corners (2016)",
   "url": "https://jasonlefkowitz.net/2016/09/why-airplane-windows-have-round-corners/"
  },
  {
   "claim": "The metal around the corners took two to three times more stress than the rest of the cabin. Later aircraft got rounded or oval windows",
   "source": "Yahoo News UK, The alarming reason plane windows were changed from square to round",
   "url": "https://uk.news.yahoo.com/alarming-reason-plane-windows-were-111101276.html"
